<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Bylaws of {{company_name}}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary-text: #111111;
      --muted-text: #555555;
      --border-color: #cccccc;
      --section-border: #e0e0e0;
      --heading-font: "Georgia", "Times New Roman", serif;
      --body-font: "Times New Roman", serif;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 40px;
      font-family: var(--body-font);
      font-size: 12pt;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--primary-text);
      background: #ffffff;
    }

    .document {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    h1, h2, h3, h4 {
      font-family: var(--heading-font);
      margin-top: 1.2em;
      margin-bottom: 0.4em;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      font-size: 18pt;
    }

    h2 {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 14pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: 12.5pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h4 {
      font-size: 12pt;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0.3em 0;
    }

    .center {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .muted {
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .article {
      margin-top: 1.5em;
      padding-top: 1em;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border);
      page-break-inside: avoid;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-weight: bold;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .small-caps {
      font-variant: small-caps;
    }

    .block {
      margin-top: 0.3em;
      margin-bottom: 0.5em;
    }

    .page-break {
      page-break-before: always;
    }

    .signature-section {
      margin-top: 3em;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      padding-top: 1.5em;
    }

    .signature-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 40px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .signature-block {
      flex: 1 1 220px;
      min-width: 220px;
    }

    .signature-line {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      height: 1.8em;
      margin-bottom: 0.2em;
    }

    .signature-label {
      font-size: 10pt;
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .execution-note {
      margin-bottom: 1em;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
    }

    .meta-header {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 1em;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .title-block {
      margin-bottom: 1.5em;
    }

    .title-block p {
      text-align: center;
      margin: 0.2em 0;
    }

    .bold {
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 0.5em 0;
      padding-left: 2em;
    }

    li {
      margin: 0.3em 0;
    }

    @media print {
      body {
        padding: 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="document">
    <!-- Title / Meta -->
    <div class="title-block">
      <h1>BYLAWS</h1>
      <h2>OF</h2>
      <h2>{{uppercase company_name}}</h2>
      <p class="muted">a {{state_of_incorporation}} corporation</p>
      <p class="muted">Adopted as of {{adoption_date}}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="meta-header">
      These Bylaws govern the internal affairs and corporate governance of {{company_name}},
      including the rights and obligations of its shareholders, directors, and officers.
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE I -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE I – OFFICES</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Registered Office.</span>
        The registered office of {{company_name}} (the "Corporation") in the State of {{state_of_incorporation}}
        shall be as set forth in the Corporation's Certificate of Incorporation, as amended
        from time to time, or at such other location within the State of {{state_of_incorporation}} as the Board
        of Directors (the "Board") may designate in accordance with applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Principal Executive Office.</span>
        The principal executive office and primary place of business of the Corporation shall
        be located {{#if principal_office_city}}in {{principal_office_city}}, {{principal_office_state}}{{else}}as designated by the Board{{/if}}, {{#if principal_office_address}}presently at {{principal_office_address}}, {{/if}}or at such other
        place or places, within or outside the State of {{state_of_incorporation}}, as may from time to time be
        determined by resolution of the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Other Offices.</span>
        The Corporation may also have such other offices, within or outside the State of {{state_of_incorporation}},
        as the Board may from time to time determine or the business of the Corporation may require.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE II -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE II – SHARE CAPITAL</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Authorized Capital.</span>
        The Corporation is authorized to issue {{authorized_shares}} shares of
        Common Stock, par value ${{par_value}} per share, as set forth in the Corporation's Certificate
        of Incorporation. The powers, designations, preferences, and rights, and the qualifications,
        limitations, and restrictions thereof, shall be as set forth therein and as provided by
        the {{state_of_incorporation}} General Corporation Law ("{{state_abbreviation}}GCL").
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Issuance of Shares.</span>
        Shares of the Corporation may be issued for such lawful consideration, at such times, and
        upon such terms as shall be determined from time to time by the Board, subject to the
        provisions of the Certificate of Incorporation and applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Shareholder Ownership Structure.</span>
        As of the date of adoption of these Bylaws, the ownership structure of the issued and
        outstanding Common Stock is as follows, subject to adjustment and future issuances:
      </p>

      <ul>
        {{#if shareholders}}
          {{#each shareholders}}
            <li>{{this.name}} – {{this.shares}} shares ({{this.percentage}}%)</li>
          {{/each}}
        {{else}}
          <li>Invero Business Trust – 60,000,000 shares (60%)</li>
          <li>Torrance Stroman – 20,000,000 shares (20%)</li>
          <li>Unissued authorized Common Stock – 20,000,000 shares (20%) reserved for equity
            incentive plans, executive and employee issuances, advisors, and future financing transactions.</li>
        {{/if}}
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4. Form of Shares.</span>
        Shares of the Corporation may be certificated or uncertificated, as determined by the Board,
        and shall be recorded in the books of the Corporation as required by law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5. Transfer of Shares.</span>
        Transfers of shares shall be made on the books of the Corporation only upon receipt of
        proper transfer instructions and compliance with any applicable restrictions, including
        those set forth in shareholder agreements, equity plans, or applicable securities laws.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE III -->
    <div class="article page-break">
      <h3>ARTICLE III – MEETINGS OF SHAREHOLDERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Annual Meetings.</span>
        An annual meeting of shareholders shall be held each year at such date, time, and place,
        within or outside the State of {{state_of_incorporation}}, as shall be fixed by the Board. At such annual
        meeting, shareholders shall elect directors and transact such other business as may properly
        come before the meeting.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Special Meetings.</span>
        Special meetings of the shareholders may be called at any time by the Board, the Chair of
        the Board, or the Chief Executive Officer (the "CEO"), and shall be called by the Secretary
        upon the written request of shareholders holding such percentage of the outstanding shares
        as may be required by the Certificate of Incorporation or applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Place and Means of Meetings.</span>
        Meetings of shareholders shall be held at such place, within or outside the State of {{state_of_incorporation}},
        as may be designated in the notice of meeting or solely by means of remote communication
        as permitted by applicable law and determined by the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4. Notice of Meetings.</span>
        Written notice stating the date, time, place (or means of remote communication), and, in the
        case of a special meeting, the purpose or purposes of the meeting, shall be given not less
        than ten (10) nor more than sixty (60) days prior to the meeting to each shareholder entitled
        to vote thereat, except as otherwise provided by law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5. Quorum.</span>
        Except as otherwise provided by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws, a
        majority of the shares entitled to vote, present in person or represented by proxy, shall
        constitute a quorum at any meeting of shareholders.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6. Voting.</span>
        Except as otherwise provided by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws, each
        outstanding share entitled to vote shall be entitled to one (1) vote upon each matter submitted
        to a vote of shareholders. Unless otherwise required by law, the Certificate of Incorporation,
        or these Bylaws, action shall be approved if the votes cast in favor exceed the votes cast against.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7. Proxies.</span>
        A shareholder may vote in person or by proxy executed in writing or by electronic transmission,
        by the shareholder or by such shareholder's duly authorized attorney-in-fact, in accordance
        with applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8. Action Without a Meeting.</span>
        Any action required or permitted to be taken at a meeting of shareholders may be taken without
        a meeting, without prior notice, and without a vote, if a consent in writing or by electronic
        transmission, setting forth the action so taken, is signed or otherwise approved by shareholders
        having not less than the minimum number of votes that would be necessary to authorize or take
        such action at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote thereon were present and voted.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE IV -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE IV – BOARD OF DIRECTORS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. General Powers.</span>
        The business and affairs of the Corporation shall be managed under the direction of the Board,
        which shall exercise all such powers of the Corporation and do all such lawful acts and things
        as are not by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws directed or required to be
        exercised or done by the shareholders.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Number and Qualifications.</span>
        The number of directors constituting the entire Board shall be fixed from time to time by
        resolution of the Board, but shall not be less than one (1). Directors need not be shareholders
        of the Corporation unless otherwise required by resolution of the Board or the Certificate
        of Incorporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Election and Term.</span>
        Directors shall be elected at the annual meeting of shareholders and shall hold office until
        their successors are duly elected and qualified or until their earlier resignation, removal,
        or death.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4. Regular Meetings.</span>
        Regular meetings of the Board shall be held at such times and places as may from time to time
        be fixed by resolution of the Board or by the Chair of the Board. No additional notice of such
        regular meetings shall be required.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5. Special Meetings.</span>
        Special meetings of the Board may be called by the Chair of the Board, the CEO, or by any two
        (2) directors then in office. Notice of any special meeting of the Board shall be given to each
        director at least twenty-four (24) hours prior to the meeting, unless such notice period is
        waived by the directors.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6. Quorum and Voting.</span>
        A majority of the directors then in office shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of
        business. The act of a majority of the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is
        present shall be the act of the Board, unless a greater number is required by law, the
        Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7. Action Without a Meeting.</span>
        Any action required or permitted to be taken at a meeting of the Board or of any committee
        thereof may be taken without a meeting if all members of the Board or such committee consent
        thereto in writing or by electronic transmission, and such writing or writings or electronic
        transmissions are filed with the minutes of proceedings of the Board or committee.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8. Committees.</span>
        The Board may designate one or more committees, each consisting of one or more directors, and
        may delegate to any such committee any of the authority of the Board to the extent permitted
        by law. Each such committee shall keep regular minutes of its meetings and report its actions
        to the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 9. Resignation and Removal.</span>
        Any director may resign at any time by delivering written or electronic notice to the Board,
        the Chair, or the Secretary. Any director or the entire Board may be removed with or without
        cause by the holders of a majority of the shares then entitled to vote at an election of
        directors, subject to any limitations set forth in the Certificate of Incorporation or
        applicable law.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE V -->
    <div class="article page-break">
      <h3>ARTICLE V – OFFICERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Officers.</span>
        The officers of the Corporation shall include, at a minimum, a Chief Executive Officer
        ("CEO"), a Chief Financial Officer ("CFO"), and a Secretary. The Corporation may also have
        such other officers as the Board may deem appropriate, including without limitation a
        Chief Technology Officer ("CTO"), Chief Experience Officer ("CXO"), and such vice presidents
        and assistant officers as the Board may designate from time to time.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Appointment and Term.</span>
        The officers of the Corporation shall be appointed by the Board and shall hold office at the
        pleasure of the Board and until their successors are duly appointed and qualified or until
        their earlier resignation, removal, or death.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Removal.</span>
        Any officer may be removed, with or without cause, by the Board at any time, without
        prejudice to the contractual rights, if any, of the person so removed.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4. Chief Executive Officer.</span>
        The CEO shall be the chief executive officer of the Corporation and shall, subject to the
        oversight of the Board, have general supervision, direction, and control over the business,
        operations, and affairs of the Corporation. The CEO shall have authority to implement and
        enforce executive performance standards, meeting attendance requirements, and operational
        directives consistent with these Bylaws and any resolutions of the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5. Chief Financial Officer.</span>
        The CFO shall be the chief financial officer of the Corporation and shall have primary
        responsibility for the financial affairs of the Corporation, including oversight of
        accounting, budgeting, reporting, and treasury functions, subject to the direction of
        the CEO and the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6. Chief Technology Officer.</span>
        The CTO, if appointed, shall be responsible for the technological strategy, product and
        platform engineering, infrastructure, and related functions of the Corporation, subject
        to the direction of the CEO and the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7. Chief Experience Officer.</span>
        The CXO, if appointed, shall be responsible for overseeing customer, driver, merchant,
        and user experience across all {{company_name}} platforms and services, subject to the direction
        of the CEO and the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8. Secretary.</span>
        The Secretary shall keep, or cause to be kept, the minutes of all meetings of the Board,
        committees of the Board, and shareholders, and shall be responsible for maintaining
        corporate records, giving notices of meetings, and performing such other duties as may
        be prescribed by the Board or the CEO.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VI -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE VI – EXECUTIVE ATTENDANCE, ACCOUNTABILITY, COMPENSATION ADJUSTMENTS, AND DISCIPLINE</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Mandatory Executive Meetings.</span>
        All executive officers of the Corporation, including without limitation the CEO, CFO, CTO,
        CXO, and any other C-level or senior executive officers, are required to attend the following
        meetings unless excused in advance:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Executive leadership meetings and strategic planning sessions;</li>
        <li>Mandatory operational and performance review meetings designated by the CEO;</li>
        <li>Crisis-response or emergency meetings designated as mandatory by the CEO or the Board;</li>
        <li>Meetings of the Board at which their attendance is requested by the Board or the CEO.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Notice of Absence.</span>
        Executives shall provide reasonable advance notice if they are unable to attend a mandatory
        meeting. Failure to provide such notice shall constitute an unexcused absence. The CEO, or
        such other officer or committee as the Board may designate, shall determine whether an absence
        is excused or unexcused.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. No-Call / No-Show.</span>
        Any failure by an executive to attend a mandatory meeting without prior notice (a "no-call /
        no-show") shall be deemed a material breach of the executive's duties and responsibilities to
        the Corporation and may subject the executive to immediate disciplinary review and remedial action.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4. Compensation Adjustments.</span>
        In connection with unexcused absences, no-call / no-show incidents, or other failures to
        perform executive duties, the Corporation may implement non-punitive, performance-based adjustments
        to executive compensation, which may include, without limitation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Reduction, suspension, or forfeiture of monthly executive stipends;</li>
        <li>Reduction, suspension, or forfeiture of performance bonuses or incentive compensation;</li>
        <li>Suspension or adjustment of executive perquisites or non-salary benefits;</li>
        <li>Delay, reduction, or suspension of equity vesting schedules, to the extent permitted by
          the applicable equity plan and award agreements;</li>
        <li>Temporary limitation or reallocation of executive authority, roles, or responsibilities.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        Such compensation adjustments shall not be deemed "fines" or penalties, but rather lawful
        adjustments to reflect the extent of performance and fulfillment of executive duties.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5. Executive Discipline.</span>
        In addition to compensation adjustments, the CEO, subject to the oversight of the Board, or
        the Board directly, may impose disciplinary actions on executives for repeated or significant
        violations of their duties, including, without limitation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Written warnings or formal reprimands;</li>
        <li>Placement on performance improvement plans with defined milestones;</li>
        <li>Temporary suspension from certain duties or authority;</li>
        <li>Reassignment or reduction in executive role;</li>
        <li>Recommendation to the Board for removal from office or termination of employment for cause.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6. Escalation and Board Review.</span>
        Two (2) or more unexcused absences or no-call / no-show incidents by an executive within
        any ninety (90) day period shall trigger mandatory review by the Board (or a committee thereof),
        which may determine whether additional compensation adjustments, disciplinary actions, or removal
        for cause are warranted.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7. Recordkeeping.</span>
        The Secretary, or such other officer as the CEO may designate, shall maintain an Executive
        Compliance Log documenting attendance at mandatory meetings, notices of absences, determinations
        of excused or unexcused absences, no-call / no-show incidents, and any related compensation
        adjustments or disciplinary actions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VII -->
    <div class="article page-break">
      <h3>ARTICLE VII – INDEMNIFICATION</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Indemnification.</span>
        To the fullest extent permitted by the {{state_abbreviation}}GCL, the Corporation shall indemnify any person who
        is or was a director or officer of the Corporation, or who is or was serving at the request
        of the Corporation as a director, officer, employee, or agent of another corporation,
        partnership, joint venture, trust, or other enterprise, against any and all expenses,
        liabilities, and losses reasonably incurred by such person in connection with any threatened,
        pending, or completed action, suit, or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative,
        or investigative.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Advancement of Expenses.</span>
        Expenses (including attorneys' fees) incurred by an indemnified person in defending or
        investigating a proceeding shall be advanced by the Corporation prior to the final disposition
        of such proceeding upon receipt of an undertaking by or on behalf of such person to repay
        such amount if it shall ultimately be determined that such person is not entitled to be
        indemnified by the Corporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Non-Exclusivity.</span>
        The rights to indemnification and advancement of expenses set forth in this Article shall not
        be exclusive of any other rights which any person may have or hereafter acquire under any
        statute, provision of the Certificate of Incorporation, agreement, vote of shareholders or
        disinterested directors, or otherwise.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VIII -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE VIII – CORPORATE RECORDS AND SEAL</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Records.</span>
        The Corporation shall maintain accurate and complete books and records of account, minutes
        of the proceedings of its shareholders, Board, and committees of the Board, and a record
        of its shareholders, all in such form and manner as required by law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Corporate Seal.</span>
        The Corporation may adopt a corporate seal in such form as the Board may determine. The
        absence of a corporate seal on any document shall not affect its validity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE IX -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE IX – CONTRACTS, CHECKS, AND TRANSFERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Contracts.</span>
        The Board may authorize any officer or officers, or agent or agents, to enter into any contract
        or execute and deliver any instrument in the name of and on behalf of the Corporation, and such
        authority may be general or confined to specific instances.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Checks and Drafts.</span>
        All checks, drafts, or other orders for the payment of money, notes, or other evidences of
        indebtedness issued in the name of the Corporation shall be signed by such officer or officers,
        or agent or agents, of the Corporation and in such manner as shall from time to time be
        determined by resolution of the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3. Transfer of Securities.</span>
        Any shares or other securities owned by the Corporation may be transferred, assigned, or
        endorsed for transfer on behalf of the Corporation by such officer or officers, or agent
        or agents, as the Board may authorize.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE X -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE X – FISCAL YEAR</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Fiscal Year.</span>
        The fiscal year of the Corporation shall be {{#if fiscal_year}}{{fiscal_year}}{{else}}fixed by resolution of the Board and may be
        changed by the Board from time to time as it deems appropriate{{/if}}.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE XI -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE XI – AMENDMENTS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. Amendments by the Board.</span>
        The Board shall have the power to adopt, amend, or repeal these Bylaws, subject to any
        limitations set forth in the Certificate of Incorporation, these Bylaws, or applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Amendments by Shareholders.</span>
        The shareholders may adopt, amend, or repeal these Bylaws by the affirmative vote of the
        holders of a majority of the shares entitled to vote thereon, unless a greater vote is
        required by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE XII -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE XII – CEO AUTHORITY AND CORPORATE CONDUCT</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1. CEO Authority.</span>
        Subject to the oversight of the Board, the CEO shall have full authority over the day-to-day
        management and operation of the Corporation, including without limitation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Implementation of strategic and operational plans approved by the Board;</li>
        <li>Supervision of executive officers and senior management;</li>
        <li>Enforcement of executive attendance, accountability, and performance standards as set
          forth in these Bylaws;</li>
        <li>Issuance of operational directives binding on executives and employees, consistent with
          applicable law and Board resolutions;</li>
        <li>Initiation of disciplinary processes and recommendations to the Board regarding the
          appointment, evaluation, and removal of officers.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2. Corporate Conduct.</span>
        All directors, officers, employees, and agents of the Corporation shall perform their duties
        in good faith, in a manner they reasonably believe to be in the best interests of the
        Corporation, and with the care an ordinarily prudent person in a like position would use
        under similar circumstances, consistent with applicable law, the Certificate of Incorporation,
        these Bylaws, and the Corporation's internal policies and codes of conduct.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- SIGNATURE SECTION -->
    <div class="signature-section page-break">
      <p class="execution-note">
        IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the undersigned, being all of the duly appointed and acting members of
        the Board of Directors of {{company_name}}, hereby adopt the foregoing Bylaws as the Bylaws of
        the Corporation, effective as of {{adoption_date}}.
      </p>

      {{#if signers}}
        {{#each signers}}
          {{#if @first}}
            <div class="signature-row">
          {{/if}}
          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{this.name}}<br />
              {{this.title}}
            </div>
          </div>
          {{#unless @last}}
            {{#if (eq (mod @index 2) 1)}}
              </div><div class="signature-row">
            {{/if}}
          {{else}}
            </div>
          {{/unless}}
        {{/each}}
      {{else}}
        <div class="signature-row">
          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{ceo_name}}<br />
              Chief Executive Officer &amp; Director
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{cfo_name}}<br />
              Chief Financial Officer
            </div>
          </div>

          {{#if cxo_name}}
          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{cxo_name}}<br />
              Chief Experience Officer
            </div>
          </div>
          {{/if}}
        </div>

        <div class="signature-row">
          {{#if secretary_name}}
          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{secretary_name}}<br />
              {{#if secretary_title}}{{secretary_title}}{{else}}Secretary{{/if}}
            </div>
          </div>
          {{/if}}

          {{#if additional_director_name}}
          <div class="signature-block">
            <div class="signature-line"></div>
            <div class="signature-label">
              {{additional_director_name}}<br />
              Director
            </div>
          </div>
          {{/if}}
        </div>
      {{/if}}

      <p class="execution-note">
        Executed and acknowledged via the {{company_name}} Executive Portal e-signature workflow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
